BT 1 0 0 1 0 99 Tm 12 TL /F2 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Architecture Selection: We chose Layered Architecture for the Customizable Subscription Box Scheduler.) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( The) Tj T* -0.110746 Tw (presentation layer handles subscriber and staff interactions, the business layer contains customization and pause/skip rules, and) Tj T* 0 Tw (the data/external-service layer provides persistence, payment, catalog and fulfillment capabilities. First, this separation of) Tj T* (concerns makes scenario-specific rules such as the 48-hour customization cutoff easier to validate and maintain. Second, clear) Tj T* (boundaries make integration between subscriptions, payments, product catalog information and fulfillment operations) Tj T* -0.008247 Tw (predictable without the operational overhead of microservices. For security, direct client access to persistent data is avoided and) Tj T* 0 Tw (business-layer authorization and validation can protect state changes. For performance, the main workflow avoids unnecessary) Tj T* (distributed calls, while fulfillment/export processing can be handled by its dedicated component. This supports the provided) Tj T* (target of exporting shipping labels for 10,000 monthly boxes in under one minute.) Tj T* ET
